# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hotel backend — module-local configuration
#
# ConfigModule loads this file first, then falls back to apps/api/.env for the
# ~120 platform-wide values (Redis, Kafka brokers, JWT secret, region config)
# that every service shares. Only variables this module owns belong here.
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Anything set here overrides the platform file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dedicated database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hotel owns its data. These HOTEL_DB_* values take precedence over
# the shared DB_* ones; any left unset falls back to the platform database, so a
# partial override is a valid way to run against shared Postgres with a
# different database name.
#
# The schema inside is always `hotel` — that is fixed in the module, not
# configurable, so the same entity definitions work whether this points at a
# dedicated instance or at the shared one.
# Defaults to the module's own Postgres on :5438, brought up by
#   docker compose --profile isolated up -d
# To run against shared Postgres instead, set port 5432 and the postgres
# superuser — the schema name is unchanged either way.
HOTEL_DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
HOTEL_DB_PORT=5438
HOTEL_DB_USER=hotel_user
HOTEL_DB_PASSWORD=change_me_in_development
HOTEL_DB_NAME=kartseek_hotel

# ── Schema source ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off, in every environment including this one. The schema comes from
# `migrations/` and nothing else:
#
#     cd modules/hotel/backend && npm run migration:show && npm run migration:run
#
# Auto-sync is a convenience for iterating on entities, not a deployment path:
# it rewrites the schema from the entity definitions on every boot, and
# annotating an existing column is enough to make it DROP and recreate that
# column — which empties it. Set this to true deliberately, for one session,
# and never against a database whose rows you want to keep. With
# NODE_ENV=production the service refuses to boot with it on at all
# (assertSynchronizeAllowed, @app/database).
DB_SYNCHRONIZE=false

# ── Transport ports ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept identical to the values the API gateway's client registrations default
# to. Changing one here means changing HOTEL_TCP_PORT
# on the gateway side too, or calls will silently go to the wrong place.
HOTEL_SERVICE_PORT=3035
HOTEL_TCP_PORT=4025
